      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In that case, you can use the \"Pearson's formula\" for calculating safety stock. It combines lead time variability and demand variability using the following formula: Safety Stock = (Lead Time Std. Dev. x Demand Std. Dev.) / Service Level. This formula assumes a normal distribution of demand, a normal distribution of lead times, and a constant demand rate. You can use Excel to calculate your safety stock based on your given data.",
